    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "but there is no \"resting\" when the person who is supposed to rest is just gone. it's like observing a void. if the consciousness is just dissolving, then the thing that's supposed to \"feel better\" or \"seek safety\" isn't even real anymore. it's just a hollow shell. doesn't it seem more logical that if the self is already disappearing, there's no reason to keep fighting to stay in a body that doesn't even feel like mine?",
